  "created": "2026-11-07T10:30:17.813Z",
  "description": "\"Listen to this article\" for Umbraco 17 and 18. Drop one ViewComponent line into any template and pass the text to read: visitors get an accessible audio player (play/pause, speed, progress, resume, download). Free and offline by default - the Browser voice needs no keys, no files and no outbound traffic - with optional server-side voices from an OpenAI-compatible API or the Piper / Kokoro add-on packages. Generated audio is cached on disk and reused, built in the background (never inside the page render), and governed from a backoffice workspace: voice mapping per culture, pronunciation rules, cache browser with regenerate / delete, plus an Audio content app. Cross-database (SQL Server, SQLite, PostgreSQL), Windows + Linux + Docker. Installs and uninstalls cleanly - it self-wires its services, migration and backoffice UI, so no host Program.cs changes are needed.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "uTPro.Feature.TextToSpeech",
  "isPrerelease": false,
